   "source": [
    "# Material-Level Analysis: Enriched Perovskite Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Abstract\n",
    "This notebook provides a deep dive into the chemical space of the perovskite materials used in this research. We analyze the stoichiometric validity, atomic properties, and physics-based stability indicators ($t$ and $\\mu$) that determine the feasibility of a 3D crystal lattice.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Research Strategy\n",
    "1.  **Data Quality:** Enforce the $ABX_3$ stoichiometric rules.\n",
    "2.  **Atomic Descriptors:** Map ionic radii and electronegativity to site-specific positions.\n",
    "3.  **Stability Mapping:** Visualize the Goldschmidt Tolerance Factor vs. Octahedral Factor."
   ],
   "id": "intro"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:38.835344Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:38.745921Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Force white background for academic presentation\n",
    "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"white\", palette=\"muted\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_p = pd.read_parquet('../data/enriched_perovskites.parquet')\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset contains {len(df_p)} unique stoichiometric perovskites.\")"
   ],
   "id": "setup",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Dataset contains 889 unique stoichiometric perovskites.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 1
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Structural Stability: The Perovskite Window\n",
    "The **Goldschmidt Tolerance Factor ($t$)** and the **Octahedral Factor ($\\mu$)** define the boundaries where a 3D perovskite can exist. Generally, $0.8 < t < 1.0$ is the stable region for cubic structures."
   ],
   "id": "stability_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:38.947026Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:38.856155Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6), facecolor='white')\n",
    "ax = sns.scatterplot(data=df_p, x='tolerance_factor', y='octahedral_factor', hue='band_gap', palette='magma', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('white')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Draw the 'Stability Window'\n",
    "plt.axvspan(0.8, 1.05, color='green', alpha=0.1, label='Stable 3D Region')\n",
    "plt.title(\"The Perovskite Stability Window\", fontsize=15)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Goldschmidt Tolerance Factor (t)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Octahedral Factor (μ)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "stability_plot",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 900x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ],
      "image/png": ""
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data",
     "jetTransient": {
      "display_id": null
     }
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 2
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Electronic Property Analysis: Band Gap Trends\n",
    "We investigate how the electronegativity of the B-site (Pb) and C-site (I, Br, Cl) influences the optical band gap."
   ],
   "id": "electronic_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:39.030718Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-20T10:54:38.972735Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5), facecolor='white')\n",
    "ax = sns.boxplot(data=df_p, x='C_1', y='band_gap', palette='Set3')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('white')\n",
    "plt.title(\"Band Gap Distribution by Primary Anion (C-site)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Primary Halogen\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Band Gap (eV)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "electronic_plot",
